  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Fan Tan (Sevens). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Fan Tan, also widely known as 'Sevens', 'Domino', or 'Parliament', is a classic layout-based card game where the objective is to be the first to get rid of all your cards. Players build upon a central layout of cards, starting with the Sevens and expanding outward to the Ace and Two in each suit. It is a game of both luck and light strategy, as players can choose to hold back key 'blocking' cards to prevent opponents from playing.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to shed all cards from your hand.',
    gameplay: "1. Starting: The player to the dealer's left (or the holder of the 7 of Diamonds in some variants) begins.\n2. Valid Plays: You can only play a card if it is:\n   nd A Seven (starts a new row for a suit).\n   nd One higher or one lower than a card already in the layout (e.g., if the 7 of Hearts is on the table, you can play the 6 or 8 of Hearts).\n3. Sequencing: Suits build up from 7 to Ace and down from 7 to 2.\n4. Passing: If you cannot play a valid card, you MUST pass. In some groups, you must pay a fine (one chip) into a pot.",
    keyRules: [
      'No skipping: You cannot play an 8 unless the 7 of that suit is present.',
      'Must play: If you have a legal move, you cannot pass.',
      'Table Layout: Cards are arranged in four rows, one for each suit.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '3 to 8 players. 4 to 6 is considered optimal.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack. Cards rank A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6-5-4-3-2 (Ace high).',
      equipment: 'Cards only.',
      dealing: "Dealer shuffles and player to dealer's right may cut. Dealer deals all cards one at a time, clockwise, starting with player to dealer's left. Some players may have one more card than others - this does not matter.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Starting: The player to the dealer's left (or the holder of the 7 of Diamonds in some variants) begins.\n2. Valid Plays: You can only play a card if it is:\n   nd A Seven (starts a new row for a suit).\n   nd One higher or one lower than a card already in the layout (e.g., if the 7 of Hearts is on the table, you can play the 6 or 8 of Hearts).\n3. Sequencing: Suits build up from 7 to Ace and down from 7 to 2.\n4. Passing: If you cannot play a valid card, you MUST pass. In some groups, you must pay a fine (one chip) into a pot.",
